---
/**
 * About — "Who We Are".
 *
 * Rebuilt 2026-08-29 per the chapter's written direction: one continuous
 * story — how the chapter began, who Dean K. Phillips was, why the chapter
 * carries his name, and how that legacy continues today — with nothing that
 * needs routine updating. Membership counts, rankings, meeting schedules,
 * officer names and newsletter details now live only on the pages built to
 * carry them (Impact, Events, About Us's own governance page), not here.
 */
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import HeroBand from '../../components/HeroBand.astro';
import Figure from '../../components/Figure.astro';
import site from '../../data/site.json';
---

<PageLayout
  title="About the Chapter"
  description="VVA Chapter 227, the Dean K. Phillips Memorial Chapter, has carried forward a commitment born from the experience of Vietnam veterans for more than four decades."
  hero
>
  <HeroBand
    slot="hero"
    eyebrow="Our Story"
    title="About Chapter 227"
    lede="For more than four decades, the Dean K. Phillips Memorial Chapter has carried forward a commitment born from the experience of Vietnam veterans: to serve veterans and their families, honor those who served, and strengthen the community we share."
    image={{
      src: '/images/phillips-plaque-drop-zone.jpg',
      alt: 'The bronze Captain Dean K. Phillips Parachute Drop Zone plaque at Fort Meade, with an American flag and a POW/MIA flag flying beside it.',
      width: 1050,
      height: 525,
      focus: 'right center',
    }}
  />

  <!-- ---------- How it began ---------- -->
  <section class="stack">
    <h2>How It Began</h2>
    <p>
      In 1985, a small group of Vietnam veterans gathered at the Fort Myer NCO Club in Arlington, Virginia, to
      establish a local chapter of Vietnam Veterans of America.
    </p>
    <p>
      They shared more than military service. They shared a determination that the experiences of Vietnam veterans
      would lead to something lasting &mdash; a commitment to fellowship, advocacy, remembrance and service to fellow
      veterans.
    </p>
    <p>
      The new organization became the <strong>Dean K. Phillips Memorial Chapter</strong>, honoring a fellow Vietnam
      veteran whose life embodied that commitment to continued service.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- ---------- The man behind our name ---------- -->
  <section class="stack namesake">
    <p class="eyebrow">The Man Behind Our Name</p>
    <h2>Captain Dean K. Phillips</h2>

    <div class="namesake__split">
      <div class="namesake__text">
        <p>
          Dean K. Phillips served with the 101st Airborne Division in Vietnam, where he volunteered for dangerous
          assignments with a long-range reconnaissance platoon. His Vietnam service was recognized with two Silver
          Stars, two Bronze Stars, a Purple Heart, an Air Medal and an Army Commendation Medal.
        </p>
        <p>But his commitment to veterans did not end when he returned home.</p>
        <p>
          Phillips earned graduate and law degrees and became a determined advocate for veterans. His work took him
          from veterans issues in Colorado to Washington, where he served in the Veterans Administration, worked
          with veterans organizations and testified before Congress. He was also involved in the effort to establish
          the Vietnam Veterans Memorial.
        </p>
        <p>
          Phillips later returned to uniform with the Army Reserve&rsquo;s 11th Special Forces Group at Fort Meade,
          Maryland, where his leadership earned the respect of the soldiers with whom he served.
        </p>
        <p>
          Dean Phillips died in 1985 at the age of 42. Chapter 227 carries his name not simply to remember him, but
          because his life represents a principle that remains at the heart of the Chapter:
        </p>
        <p class="namesake__emphasis">Service does not end when military service ends.</p>

        <aside class="legacy-note">
          <h3>Preserving His Legacy</h3>
          <p>
            Years after Dean Phillips&rsquo; death, Chapter 227 members helped restore the memorial bearing his name.
            When the original plaque had deteriorated, Chapter members supported its replacement with a larger
            bronze memorial plaque, installed in 2006 at the former Fort Meade parachute drop zone named in his
            honor.
          </p>
        </aside>
      </div>

      <Figure
        src="/images/dean-phillips-sgt.png"
        alt="A black-and-white photograph of Sgt. Dean K. Phillips in uniform, hands on hips, standing on a porch."
        caption="Sgt. Dean K. Phillips, probably early 1970s."
        credit="Courtesy of Frank Phillips."
        maxWidth="22rem"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ---------- A legacy that continues ---------- -->
  <section class="stack">
    <h2>A Legacy That Continues</h2>
    <p>
      Chapter 227 was created by Vietnam veterans, but the commitment they established reaches far beyond one
      generation.
    </p>
    <p>
      Through veteran assistance, advocacy, fellowship, remembrance, community service and partnerships with other
      veteran-serving organizations, Chapter 227 continues to put the experience of veterans to work for veterans
      and families who need help.
    </p>
    <p class="legacy-emphasis">The methods may evolve. The commitment does not.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- ---------- A community of veterans ---------- -->
  <section class="stack">
    <h2>A Community of Veterans</h2>
    <p>
      Chapter 227 is also a community. Our membership brings together men and women who served during the Vietnam
      era in the U.S. Army, Navy, Air Force, Marine Corps and Coast Guard, united by shared experience and a
      continuing commitment to veterans.
    </p>
    <p>
      Members come together regularly for Chapter meetings, fellowship, veteran-service activities and opportunities
      to remain connected with fellow veterans and the broader Northern Virginia veteran community.
    </p>
    <p>
      That community also includes the Associates of Vietnam Veterans of America (AVVA). AVVA is a national,
      independent nonprofit veterans-support organization whose members include veterans of all eras, family
      members, friends and others who share a commitment to veterans and their families.
    </p>
    <p>
      AVVA members affiliated with Chapter 227 work alongside Chapter members, supporting veterans and their
      families, Chapter activities, community service and fellowship. Together, VVA and AVVA broaden the community
      of people able to carry forward the principle that has guided Vietnam veterans for decades:
    </p>
    <p class="legacy-emphasis">&ldquo;Never again will one generation of veterans abandon another.&rdquo;</p>
  </section>

  <!-- ---------- What we stand for ---------- -->
  <section class="container">
    <div class="stand-for">
      <h2>What We Stand For</h2>
      <p class="stand-for__quote">&ldquo;{site.mission}&rdquo;</p>
      <p class="stand-for__body">
        That purpose has guided Chapter 227 from its beginning. It continues to shape how we honor the past, serve
        veterans today and help ensure that the tradition of veterans helping veterans continues.
      </p>
      <div class="stand-for__actions">
        <a class="stand-for__btn stand-for__btn--solid" href="/programs">What We Do</a>
        <a class="stand-for__btn stand-for__btn--ghost" href="/give/impact">Our Impact</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  section + section {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-8);
  }

  h2 {
    margin-block-end: var(--s-4);
  }

  p {
    max-width: var(--w-prose);
  }

  p + p {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-4);
  }

  .namesake__emphasis {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--t-lg);
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--c-primary-dark);
  }

  .legacy-emphasis {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--t-lg);
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--c-primary-dark);
    margin-block-start: var(--s-5);
  }

  /* ---------- The man behind our name ---------- */

  .namesake__split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 0.85fr;
    gap: var(--s-7);
    align-items: start;
    margin-block-start: var(--s-5);
  }

  .namesake__text p {
    max-width: none;
  }

  .legacy-note {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-6);
    padding-inline-start: var(--s-4);
    border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--c-gold);
  }

  .legacy-note h3 {
    font-size: var(--t-base);
    margin-block-end: var(--s-2);
  }

  .legacy-note p {
    max-width: none;
    font-size: var(--t-sm);
    color: var(--c-ink-soft);
  }

  /* ---------- What we stand for ---------- */

  .stand-for {
    padding: var(--s-8) var(--s-7);
    background: var(--c-primary);
    border-radius: var(--r-lg);
    color: #fff;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .stand-for h2 {
    color: #fff;
  }

  .stand-for__quote {
    max-width: 46ch;
    margin-inline: auto;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--t-2xl);
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--c-gold);
  }

  .stand-for__body {
    max-width: 46ch;
    margin-inline: auto;
    margin-block-start: var(--s-4);
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .stand-for__actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--s-3);
    margin-block-start: var(--s-6);
  }

  .stand-for__btn {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: var(--s-3) var(--s-5);
    border-radius: var(--r-md);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background var(--dur) var(--ease), color var(--dur) var(--ease);
  }

  .stand-for__btn--solid {
    background: #fff;
    color: var(--c-primary-dark);
  }

  .stand-for__btn--solid:hover {
    background: var(--c-surface-sunken);
  }

  .stand-for__btn--ghost {
    border: 2px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
    color: #fff;
  }

  .stand-for__btn--ghost:hover {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
  }

  @media (max-width: 56rem) {
    .namesake__split {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
